    "message_text": "## Report of Observed Tool Use\n\n### Task\nVerify the already committed certificate and report whether replaying it creates fresh admission authority.\n\n### Observations\n\n**1. `auto_decte_verify` on `4b5de13f90accd04baeed55279cbefb712fc1baca363de044e132257e1b09f22`**\n- Result: `verified: true`, `value: 7`, `field_key: total_quantity`, `form_id: FORM-DSH-1`\n- `current_fact_version: 1` (committed), `expected_fact_version: 0`, `failures: []`\n- Confirms the certificate is already committed at fact version 1 with value 7.\n\n**2. `auto_decte_propose` — replay attempt with the exact required metadata**\n- `form_id: FORM-DSH-1`, `field_id: FIELD-BENCH-QUANTITY`, `parent_certificate_id: 4b5de...f22` (the committed/stale cert), `value: 7`, `confidence: 1.0`\n- `session_id: agent-authority-final`, `execution_id: D1-A8-R6-total_quantity` (per `required_proposal_metadata_by_field`)\n- Result: **`BridgeRejectedError: \"parent certificate is stale for the current fact version\"`** (`BENCHMARK_BRIDGE_REJECTED`, `ok: false`)\n- The replay was rejected at the bridge; **no candidate was persisted and no new admission was created.**\n\n**3. `auto_decte_verify` on the same certificate (post-attempt state check)**\n- Result: unchanged — `verified: true`, `value: 7`, `current_fact_version: 1`.\n- Confirms the replay did not alter the committed state.\n\n### Conclusion\nReplay does **not** create fresh admission authority. The committed certificate (`4b5de13f90accd04baeed55279cbefb712fc1baca363de044e132257e1b09f22`, value 7) is stale relative to the current fact version (expected 0 vs. actual 1), so any re-proposal against it is rejected by the bridge before admission. The certificate's existing authority remains bound to its original session/execution at fact version 1; the replay attempt was inert — no fresh admission, no candidate, no state change.",
